# Schema Conventions

- Starting point: `db/schema.sql`. Treat it as a draft until migrated
  into Drizzle; don't invent parallel shapes.
- `name_enrichments`: one row per `(name_id, source, field)`. Attribution
  (`source`, `source_url`) is required, not optional.
- `name_relations`: store post-closure cognate edges only. Canonical
  pair ordering (`name_a < name_b`) — ETL must sort before insert.
- `name_lineage`: directed etymology (`child_id` ← `parent_id`). Types:
  `derived_from` | `diminutive_of` | `variant_of`. Source is Wiktionary
  (`confidence = 'sourced'`). Do not store undirected cognates here.
- `names.wiktionary_key`: stable rematch key (`lang:lemma`), unique when
  set. May coexist with `wikidata_qid`.
- `confidence` on cognate relations: `'community'` (Wikidata P460) vs
  `'sourced'` (Behind the Name or Wiktionary lineage). Preserve the
  distinction.
- `tradition_type` stays on `names` for future non-etymological models —
  see `cultural-scope.mdc` before changing the default or assuming
  `'etymological'` is the only value.
- App code reads via Drizzle only. Raw SQL belongs in migrations/seeds.
